  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 254 PM CDT Thu Oct 15 2026\n\nSurface high pressure gradually moves into the region Friday night \ninto Saturday morning allowing winds to drop off, skies to clear, \nand good radiational cooling. Temperatures by Saturday morning fall \ninto the upper 20s to low 30s. A Freeze Watch has been issued for \nSaturday morning to account for these low temperatures so make plans \nnow to protect any sensitive vegetation! The pressure gradient \ntightens again Saturday behind the departing high pressure leading \nto breezy winds, especially north, Saturday into Sunday. Conditions \notherwise remain dry with the surface high and an upper ridge in \nplace. Temperatures begin to rebound later Saturday into Sunday as \nsouthwest flow returns translating to gradually increasing highs \nthis weekend into early next week. Highs in the 50s Saturday become \n60s Sunday-Monday and 70s again by Tuesday. There are a few hints of \na small system near the region around Monday night but our forecast \nremains dry until mid to later next week when there is a bit more \nconsensus for returning precipitation chances though details will \ncontinue to be refined in the coming days.",
